---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'October 20, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="The privacy policy for NyankoTools, covering how we handle personal information and our use of analytics and advertising services and cookies."
>
  <h1 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="mb-8 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
    Last updated: {lastUpdated}
  </p>

  <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-8 text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-300">
    <p>
      NyankoTools (the "Site") has established this Privacy Policy to explain
      how it handles user information, including personal information, so that
      users can use the Site with confidence.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">1. Operator Information</h2>
      <p>
        The Site is operated by an individual. See the
        <a
          href="/en/about/"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          About page
        </a>
        for more details. For inquiries regarding this policy, please contact us
        using the information in Section 9 ("Contact") below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">
        2. Our Basic Policy (How Tools Process Data)
      </h2>
      <p>
        Every tool offered on the Site runs entirely as client-side processing
        within your browser. Data you enter — for text conversion, formatting,
        calculations, and the like — is never sent to the Site's servers. Your
        input is processed only within your own browser and is never stored or
        transmitted externally.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        To restore your input after a page reload or a language switch, the Site
        temporarily keeps it in your browser's session storage (it is cleared
        when you close the tab and is never sent to any server). Tools that
        handle sensitive data such as passwords or tokens do not save it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Tools that use a camera, microphone, screen sharing, or gamepad (such as
        the webcam tester, mic tester, screen recorder, and QR code reader)
        process video, audio, and input only on your device, after you grant
        permission in your browser. Nothing is sent to a server or stored by the
        Site. You can revoke permission at any time in your browser settings.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        The contact page works by opening your email app (mailto), so what you
        enter never passes through the Site's servers. Your email reaches the
        operator through your own email service and is used only to reply to
        you. Share buttons (X, Facebook, etc.) take you to the respective
        service only when you click them and send nothing automatically.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">3. Access Logs</h2>
      <p>
        The Site's hosting provider (Cloudflare) may automatically record access
        logs — such as IP address, browser type, referrer URL, and access
        timestamps — as part of its standard functionality. This information is
        used solely for security and maintenance purposes, such as preventing
        unauthorized access and keeping the Site running stably, and is not used
        to identify individuals.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">
        4. Analytics and Advertising Services
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-2">
        The Site uses Google Analytics (GA4) and Cloudflare Web Analytics as
        analytics tools to improve the Site. The Site does not currently use any
        advertising service, but in the future we may use third-party services
        such as Google AdSense to support its continued operation. If we do, we
        will update this policy beforehand.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-2">
        Google Analytics uses cookies to collect traffic data. Data collected
        through cookies is anonymous and does not identify you personally. You
        can opt out of this data collection by disabling cookies in your
        browser; please refer to your browser's help documentation for
        instructions. Cloudflare Web Analytics does not use cookies and does not
        track individuals.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-2">
        The information sent to outside providers is listed below. Neither
        includes the text or files you enter into a tool, or file names.
      </p>
      <div class="mb-2 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700">
              <th class="py-2 pr-3 font-semibold">Recipient / service</th>
              <th class="py-2 pr-3 font-semibold">Information sent</th>
              <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Purpose</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="align-top">
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
              <td class="py-2 pr-3">Google LLC (Google Analytics 4)</td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-3">
                Page URL and title, referrer, IP address, device / browser / OS
                / language, identifiers such as cookies, copy and download
                actions, and errors (tool name only)
              </td>
              <td class="py-2">Analyzing site usage and improving the tools</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
              <td class="py-2 pr-3">
                Cloudflare, Inc. (Cloudflare Web Analytics)
              </td>
              <td class="py-2 pr-3">
                Pages viewed, referrer, device / browser type, and load
                performance (no cookies)
              </td>
              <td class="py-2">Aggregating traffic and improving page speed</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="mb-2">
        URL parameters that may contain your input (
        <span class="font-mono">?text=</span>,<span class="font-mono">?q=</span>
        , <span class="font-mono">?c=</span>) are removed before being sent to
        Google Analytics. You can opt out of Google Analytics with the
        <a
          href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-blue-700 underline hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
        >
          Google Analytics opt-out add-on
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <p>
        For the terms of service and privacy policy of Google Analytics and
        Cloudflare Web Analytics, please refer to Google's and Cloudflare's
        official websites, respectively. Third-party vendors, including Google,
        may also use cookies to serve ads based on a user's visits to the Site
        and other sites. You can opt out of personalized advertising through
        Google's Ads Settings page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">5. About Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small data files that a website sends to your browser and
        that are stored on your device. The Site uses cookies through the
        analytics services described above (only Google Analytics sets cookies).
        You can refuse cookies or delete cookies already stored through your
        browser settings.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        For convenience, the Site also stores the following in your browser's
        local storage. None of it is sent to any server, and it is removed when
        you clear the site's data in your browser.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
        <li>
          Favorite tools, recently used tools (tool names only, up to 8), theme
          (light/dark), and sidebar open/closed state
        </li>
        <li>Best scores for game tools and rock-paper-scissors stats</li>
        <li>
          Issuer details you save in the Invoice Generator, and the UTM Builder
          history
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">
        6. Disclosure of Personal Information to Third Parties
      </h2>
      <p>
        The Site will not disclose any information it collects to third parties
        without the individual's consent, except in the following cases:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
        <li>When disclosure is required by law</li>
        <li>
          When disclosure is necessary to protect a person's life, body, or
          property, and obtaining consent is difficult
        </li>
        <li>
          When cooperation with a national or local government agency is
          necessary for it to carry out duties prescribed by law
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">
        7. Rights Regarding Personal Information Protection
      </h2>
      <p>
        If you reside in a jurisdiction where data protection laws such as the
        EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) or the California Consumer
        Privacy Act (CCPA) apply, you have the right to request disclosure,
        correction, or deletion of information the Site holds about you. To make
        such a request, please contact us using the information in Section 9
        ("Contact") below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">8. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The Site does not knowingly collect personal information from minors (in
        particular, children of an age at which parental consent is required).
        Minors should use the Site with the consent of a parent or guardian.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For inquiries regarding this policy, please contact us at the email
        address below.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-sm">nyankotools@gmail.com</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">
        10. Changes to This Privacy Policy
      </h2>
      <p>
        The Site may change the contents of this policy without notice in
        response to changes in law or in the services it offers. Any revised
        privacy policy takes effect as soon as it is posted on this page. We
        will announce material changes on this page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
